            "content": "# llame agent-instruction audit — 2026-08-30\n\nSix instruction files, plus the eagerly-`@`-imported set. Scores follow the\nclaude-md-improver rubric; the load figures are what actually enters context.\n\n## Context budget (the number that drives everything)\n\n| Scope | Files eagerly loaded | ~tokens |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Any conversation | `AGENTS.md` + `@README.md` + `@CONTRIBUTING.md` + auto-loaded `CLAUDE.local.md` | **15,600** |\n| Working in `apps/api` | the above + `apps/api/AGENTS.md` | **33,400** |\n| + proposed `@CODING_STANDARDS.md` | | **35,900** |\n\n`apps/api/AGENTS.md` alone is 17,700 tokens — larger than the root file, both\n`@` imports, and every other workspace file combined.\n\n## Scores\n\n| File | Lines | Score | Grade |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | :-: |\n| `AGENTS.md` (root) | 155 | 84 | B |\n| `apps/api/AGENTS.md` | 724 | 46 | D |\n| `apps/web/AGENTS.md` | 55 | 88 | B+ |\n| `apps/web/lib/api/AGENTS.md` | 39 | 90 | A- |\n| `apps/storybook/AGENTS.md` | 52 | 91 | A- |\n| `packages/ui/AGENTS.md` | 96 | 72 | B- |\n\nAverage 78.5. One file needs structural work; one needs trimming; four are fine.\n\n### `apps/api/AGENTS.md` — 46/100 (D)\n\n| Criterion | Score | Note |\n| --- | ---: | --- |\n| Commands/workflows | 17/20 | Complete and accurate |\n| Architecture clarity | 11/20 | Structure section is a single 600-word bullet; headings lie about contents |\n| Non-obvious patterns | 14/15 | The gotchas are real — that is not the problem |\n| Conciseness | 2/15 | 17.7k tokens, ~40% duplicated from OpenSpec and `.sql` headers |\n| Currency | 12/15 | Accurate but append-only; nothing is ever retired |\n| Actionability | 8/15 | Per-migration archaeology is unreachable when needed, unavoidable when not |\n\n### `packages/ui/AGENTS.md` — 72/100 (B-)\n\nCorrect and useful, but the shadcn story-transcription workflow (~55 lines:\nupstream example URLs, `curl`/`gh api` recipes, tag taxonomy, per-failure fixes)\nis a task procedure, not s